Problem #2 Report
Node Used: hostname
Compiler Version: gcc --version
Compile Flags: -Wall -Wextra -std=c11 -I…/include -O0/-O2/-O3 -lrt
Number of Repetitions: 5
Statistic Reported: Average runtime using microseconds, checksum, and nanoseconds per element
Based upon the results, we can see that the prefix sum shows differences between each optimization level. -O0 is the slowest, as it has 2.4 to 2.6 ns/element. The runtime is reduced for both -O3 and -O2, showing around 0.37 ns/element. We can also see that they are both nearly identical in performance, which may mean the compiler can’t optimize the loop beyond what one of them does. The double precision operations are slower compared to the integer operations, possibly due to a higher memory bandwidth pressure and computational cost. We can also see that the checksums match the expected values.
