Problem #3 Report
Node Used: hostname
Compiler Version: gcc --version
Compile Flags: -Wall -Wextra -std=c11 -I…/include -O3 -lrt
Number of Repetitions: 3
Statistic Reported: Average runtime in microseconds and GFLOP/s
We needed to loop six different variants of matrix multiplication, using ijk, ikj, jik, jki, kji, and kjj. Based upon the results, the fastest groups seem to be ikj and kij with about 10 to 13 GFLOPS. The slowest group is jki and kji, which both produced poorly with about 0.3 to 0.7 GFLOPS. The other two groups, ijk and jik are around 1 GFLOPS, so they are about in the middle. Each output gave a correct answer of yes as well. Overall, orders with k outermost seem to achieve high throughput and maximizes its cache reuse, compared to j outermost.
