Problem #5 Report
Node Used: hostname
Compiler Version: gcc --version
Compile Flags: -Wall -Wextra -std=c11 -I…/include -O3 -lrt
Number of Repetitions: 16
Statistic Reported: TEPS
Based on the results, we have two graphs generated being Erdos-Renyi and RMAT. Looking at Erdos-Renyi, it has 8 levels and its fraction reached is 1.000000. RMAT has 6 to 8 levels and its fraction reached 0.4814. Then, looking at the TEPS, Erdos-Renyi has about 16,700,000 inspected levels with the TEPs ranging from 118M to 122M, For RMAT, it has about 15,800,000 inspected levels and its TEPs ranges from 259M to 288M. Based on both graphs, RMAT seems to be 2.3 times faster than Erdos-Renyi. This is found by dividing the two medians from both graphs.

